ot of the officer's silhouette on the bridge, glowing floor lines.\n\n3.0s-5.0s: Hard cut to a side-profile close-up of the female officer. Cold, dim blue lighting. Her expression is resolute and slightly sorrowful. Subtle camera shake. Wind blows her ponytail slightly.\n\n5.0s-7.0s: Hard cut to pure black screen with text \"EARTH SENT THE LAST FLEET\" and \"FINAL COUNTDOWN\". Instantly cut to the deep space nebula. The massive fleet suddenly warps. A blinding spatial distortion erupts, creating hypersonic light trails and shockwaves.\n\n7.0s-9.5s: Hard cut back to the officer's side-profile close-up. A blinding white warp flash explodes from the window, completely overexposing her face with intense white light. Her hair is blown back by the blast. Camera shakes violently.\n\n9.5s-11.0s: The intense light fades back to the dark, cold blue shadow. The officer's face is illuminated only by the faint starlight, revealing a tear or a look of realization. \n\n11.0s-13.0s: Rapid hard cut to pure black screens with flashing text \"WITHOUT HER\" and \"SHE KNEW WHY\". Minimalist, cinematic typography.\n\n13.0s-15.0s: Final slam cut. The ultimate title \"THE LAST FLEET LEFT EARTH SHE WAS NOT ON BOARD\" slams onto the screen. A subtle lens flare sweeps across the dark metallic text. Hard cut to pure black.\nOverall: IMAX 70mm film grain, deep contrast, breathtaking space VFX, serious and tragic tone, NO pure white text, metallic glowing fonts.", 1344, 768, 124], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 19, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"name": "vae", "link": 20, "label": "vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "first_frame", "link": 21, "label": "first_frame", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "first_frame"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "last_frame", "link": 22, "label": "last_frame", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "last_frame"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "link": 23, "label": "prompt", "type": "STRING"